																	<a href="/forum/t-13895879/two-scp-green-light#post-4839394">Re: Two SCP green light</a>
									</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jamaisj" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6846344); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6846344&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607413971" alt="JamaisJ" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6846344)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jamaisj" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6846344); return false;" >JamaisJ</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607409105 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">08 Dec 2020 06:31</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13895879/two-scp-green-light">Two SCP green light</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4839394">
									

<p>1) The containment is a no-brainer: If they both have humanoid forms then just set a room up for them to nuzzle in. That puts him and his nullification abilities in the center of a site with no problems. After all, if he does whatever she says and she can be convinced to come in willingly, it would be easy.</p>
<p>I'd also point out that &quot;containment&quot; doesn't mean &quot;onsite&quot;. A number of SCPs are contained without forcing them into an actual site or even penned up. &quot;Containment&quot; is all about neutralizing the threat, and if that means just ensuring that the SCP has a wide berth, then so be it; whichever way is expeditious is the way The Foundation usually goes.</p>
<p>Strictly as a side note, I'd point out that a number of SCPs fall in the same category of invulnerability; if the dragon really is a Keter-level threat (and he sounds like it), then he can be dealt with either directly or by sending him to another dimension.</p>
<p>2) The monstrous forms are the problem here, just because of its two gigantic monstrous forms. However, if you point out that they prefer humanoid form then there shouldn't be a problem. The humanoid forms would also take out caspian's problem.</p>
<p>3) A better hook is &quot;love will find a way&quot;. The cool part here is that you have two different forms of immortality (long-term versus a cycle of death/renewal) and that they need to find a way to make their romance work. In the messed-up world of The Foundation, THAT is much cooler than just worrying about some relatively trivial containment issue.</p>
<p>4) As long as the two are a pair, this is technically ONE SCP (XXXX-1/XXXX-2). Just sayin'&#8230;.</p>

							</div>

								
					
